<title>USA: CMS sees 67 MW nuke at full output today.</title>
<headline>CMS sees 67 MW nuke at full output today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co, a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp, expected its 67 megawatt (MW) Big Rock Point 1 nuclear station to achieve full output later today, a company spokesman said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;It should be back up to full power this afternoon,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Big Rock Point's production was scaled back late Thursday to perform work on the reactor feed pump.</p>
<p>Big Rock Point 1 in Charlevoix, Mich., accounts for one percent of the utility's installed generation capacity.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
